er Monday, if she"}]}, {"type": "post_question", "contents": {"type": "", "content": "sick and cancelled the meeting."}}, {"type": "objective", "content": "secondary_7"}]}, {"responses": [{"correct": 0, "id": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}, {"correct": 0, "id": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "would have told"}]}, {"correct": 1, "text": "", "id": 2, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "wouldn't have told"}]}, {"correct": 0, "text": "", "id": 3, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "wouldn't had told"}]}], "id": 2, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "If he had known he was talking to the CEO, he"}]}, {"type": "post_question", "contents": {"type": "", "content": "that terrible story."}}, {"type": "objective", "content": "secondary_7"}]}], "template_override": 1, "id": 8, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " More examples of bad luck!"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\nInstructions: Click on the drop-down list. Complete the sentence by selecting the correct answer.\n"}]}]}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "type": "MT1", "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "id": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}, {"correct": 1, "id": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "free time today, does he?"}]}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "The manager doesn't have any"}]}, {"type": "objective", "content": "secondary_8"}]}, {"responses": [{"correct": 0, "id": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}, {"correct": 1, "id": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "out of business, isn't it?"}]}], "id": 1, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "That company is going"}]}, {"type": "objective", "content": "secondary_8"}]}, {"responses": [{"correct": 0, "id": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}, {"correct": 1, "id": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "position yesterday, did you?"}]}], "id": 2, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "You didn't interview for the"}]}, {"type": "objective", "content": "secondary_8"}]}], "template_override": 1, "id": 9, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Checking your information."}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\n\nInstructions: Move the words up or down <span class=\"sena-icon sena-icon-vertical-drag\"></span> to complete each sentence\n."}]}]}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "type": "RSLT", "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "id": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}, {"correct": 1, "id": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}]}], "template_override": 1, "id": 10, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}]}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "type": "DWS", "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 1, "id": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "engenn9le09ob09re7pdf01.pdf"}]}]}], "template_override": 1, "id": 11, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " If you could give advice to your younger self, what would you say?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment."}]}]}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn9le09ob09re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn9le09ob09re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn9le09ob09re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn9le09ob09re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "Yesterday was a tough day. First, in the morning, I scoped out the Corbin group and talked to an employee there named Roger, who I actually knew.  He gave me some good insight into the organization. It sounds like an interesting place.\n<br/>\nIf only I had gotten his card the first time we met, yesterday's meeting wouldn't have been so awkward.  If I'd had his card, I could have called before-hand and not seemed quite so desperate. Oh well."}, {"time": "28000", "image": "engenn9le09ob09re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "In the afternoon, I had planned to contact Durban Inc. I talked about them previously, didn't I? Anyway, while I was at Corbin, a friend sent me an email saying that Durbin had a job opening that I would be perfect for, but I needed to contact them immediately. I was so excited, but my excitement quickly turned to frustration; the position had already been filled ... that morning.\n<br/>\nI remember badgering the HR director with questions on the phone. \u201cThe position is still open, isn't it? If I send my resume now I can still be considered, can't I?  You aren't looking for anyone else, are you?\u201d It was humiliating."}, {"time": "68400", "image": "engenn9le09ob09re2img03.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "If only I had stayed home that morning, I would have gotten the email earlier.<br/>\nIf only I had talked to my source earlier in the week, I would have had a chance to apply. If only I hadn't gone to the Corbin group in the morning, I would have had a chance at this opportunity. Sometimes in life you make choices without even knowing it."}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}]}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Getting the Job You Want"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Right Choices"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Third Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are four types of conditional sentences in English:<ol><li>Zero Conditional - to talk about certainty and facts</li><li>First Conditional - to talk about real possibilities in the present or the future</li><li>Second Conditional - to talk about <span class=\"italic\">unreal</span> possibilities in the present or the future</li><li>Third Conditional - to talk about unreal <span class=\"italic\">past</span> situations</li></ol>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use third conditional to talk about unreal situations in the past. <br/>These are things that did not happen in the past. You often use the third conditional to talk about regrets."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the third conditional:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Conditional Name</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Structure</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Example</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Third \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> + Past Perfect, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">could</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">would have</span> + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If only I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had stayed</span> home that morning, I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would have gotten</span> the email earlier.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If only I had gotten his card the first time we met, yesterday's meeting wouldn't have been so awkward.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I had his card, I could have called before-hand and not seemed quite so desperate. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If only I had stayed home that morning, I would have gotten the email earlier."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If only I had talked to my source earlier in the week, I would have had a chance to apply. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If only I hadn't gone to the Corbin group in the morning, I would have had a chance at this opportunity. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Tag Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use tag questions to ask for clarification and confirmation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Question tags are short questions at the end of statements."}, {"type": "text", "content": "They are mainly used in speech when we want to:<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">clarify/confirm whether something is true or not true</span>, or</li><li><span class=\"strong\">to encourage a reply</span> from the person we are speaking to.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ol><li value=\"1\">A <span class=\"strong\">positive</span> statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> question tag.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying \u2018yes' <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>You <span class=\"strong\">were</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">weren't you?</span></li> <li>You <span class=\"strong\">are</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> you?</li> <li>She <span class=\"strong\">has</span> a brother, <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> she?</li> <li>He <span class=\"strong\">can</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> he?</li></ul></span></li></ol>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ol><li value=\"2\">A <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">positive</span> question tag.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying \u2018no'  <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>You <span class=\"strong\">weren't</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">were you? </span></li> <li>You <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">are</span> you?</li> <li>She <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> have a brother, <span class=\"strong\">does</span> she?</li> <li>He <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can</span> he?</li></ul></span> </li></ol>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If the main verb is <span class=\"italic\">to be</span> or a <span class=\"strong\">modal verb</span>, the tag will be the same. <br/>For <span class=\"strong\">all other main verbs</span>, use the tag <span class=\"italic\">do</span>/<span class=\"italic\">does </span>or <span class=\"italic\">did</span>/<span class=\"italic\">didn't</span>. <br/>Look at the examples in the chart."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He is/was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"isn't/wasn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"aren't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"can't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"couldn't we?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"won't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She has/had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't/didn't she?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He likes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You like\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You liked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"didn't you?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I talked about them previously, didn't I?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The position is still open, isn't it?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I send my resume now I can still be considered, can't I?  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You aren't looking for anyone else, are you?"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "before-hand"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in advance, earlier"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:I could have called before-hand and not seemed quite so desperate."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear stories about regret."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "insight"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "knowledge about something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He gave me some good insight into the organization."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "desperate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "having an urgent need "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I could have called before-hand and not seemed quite so desperate."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "badgering"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to bother or annoy continuously "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example :I remember badgering the HR director with questions on the phone."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "awkward"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "causing or feeling embarrassment or inconvenience"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:If only I had gotten his card the first time we met, yesterday's meeting wouldn't have been so awkward. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to scope out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to look at or over; examine"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:I scoped out the Corbin group and talked to an employee there named Roger, who I actually knew. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob09aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I use the third conditional to express regret about the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present my regrets to a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a short essay about giving advice to my younger self."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my advice with a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Imagine you have three regrets from your past you would like to change."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write sentences about your regrets using hypothetical situations in the past to explain your regrets in detail."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Then imagine you can give advice to your younger self, what would you say focusing on your three regrets?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Express your thoughts in 200 words."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your advice to a partner."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le09ob09re1img01.jpg"}]}